From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chu Qinghao <6337103+qinghao1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] bridge: publish EM score-reel digits

DispReel scores (SetValue/AddValue/ResetToZero) only queue motor pulses;
DispReel::UpdateAnimation (run by PrepareFrame) rolls them into
m_reelInfo[].currentValue, the digit DispReel::Render draws. That state
is private with no accessor, so add DispReel::GetReelValue and publish
it as buffer kind 5 (reels, stride 4: partIdx, reel, value, visible),
one row per reel. Backdrop items skip the VR part-group mask: the host
shows them on its own backglass. ABI version 2.

Target: vpinball/vpinball@64a480a96d1b972711fbb8eea014654c779b1e23

diff --git a/src/parts/dispreel.h b/src/parts/dispreel.h
index 5952a5db..34a8d31a 100644
--- a/src/parts/dispreel.h
+++ b/src/parts/dispreel.h
@@ -165,6 +165,9 @@ private:
       float   motorOffset;        // frame value of motor (where to display the reel)
    };
    ReelInfo    m_reelInfo[MAX_REELS];
+public:
+   int GetReelValue(const int reel) const { return m_reelInfo[reel].currentValue; }
+private:
 
    float       m_reeldigitwidth;  // size of the individual reel digits (in bitmap form)
    float       m_reeldigitheight;
